<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned three direct sales of paper and six repurchase agreements, whereby it had sought to drain 3.398 billion pesos from the secondary market on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    363 days   20.40 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    180 days   20.28 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days   19.54 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    450 million     77 days   20.37 pct</p>
<p>    450 million     67 days   20.22 pct</p>
<p>    650 million     53 days   20.00 pct</p>
<p>    650 million     31 days   19.84 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     15 days   19.66 pct</p>
<p>    148 million	1 day    18.89 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
